WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.030
There's no shortage of gut-churning horror
films on Netflix...but a new offering has

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.440
audiences covering their mouths, clutching
their stomachs, and even getting sick.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.700
It's safe to say The Perfection is unlike
any horror film you've ever seen before, on

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.059
Netflix, or anywhere else.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.060
But before we get too deep into the nitty-gritty,
please note: Major spoilers ahead!

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.160
The Perfection stars Allison Williams and
Logan Browning as Charlotte and Lizzie, two

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.980
cello prodigies who study at the prestigious
music school Bachoff.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.640
The film centers around Charlotte's return
to Bachoff after taking leave of absence to

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.060
look after her ailing mother.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.900
She reconnects with her mentors and soon meets
the talented musician who replaced her when

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.520
she left.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.360
That musician is Lizzie.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.980
"I'm sorry, am I the luckiest man in the world?

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.040
I don't even drink and I feel drunk.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.800
My two most perfect students together."

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.560
Based on the film's title and storyline, it's
easy to assume The Perfection will be a dark

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.770
tale of jealousy and one-upmanship...much
like Darren Aronofsky's 2010 psychological

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:05.080
thriller Black Swan, or the classic 1950 melodrama
All About Eve.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.180
But then, after the first of many plot twists,
you might mistake The Perfection for a ghoulish

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.120
outbreak drama.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.100
"What's happening?"

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.580
"Oh my god, your arm!"

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.970
But The Perfection is actually far more complex
than that, and the end result has a few far

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.640
more grotesque moments.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.620
If Twitter can be believed, the film's occasional
grizzly moments, and insane ending, are making

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.240
viewers physically ill.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.800
One Twitter user complained,

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.320
"i havent seen the whole thing but i watched
some scenes from the perfection on netflix

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.440
and it is literally making me feel sick."

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.840
Another viewer tweeted:

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:45.720
"the perfection on netflix is SICK…in a
bad way ugh my body can't move and i feel

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.460
like puking."

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.960
And yet another viewer totally agreed with
that assessment:

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.840
"Just got done eating while watching The Perfection
on Netflix and I think I’m going to puke."

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.500
But that's not to say it's a bad film by any
stretch of the imagination.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.640
Plenty of people thought The Perfection was
a gripping and original horror movie.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.280
One Twitter user breathlessly summed up her
feelings by writing:

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:13.420
"The film is sick, twisted, cunning, beautifully
made, creepy, evil, scary, funny, tragic all

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.420
at the same time.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.600
What a psychological horror thriller!!"

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.580
While many viewers found it grueling to watch
The Perfection, it reportedly wasn't the easiest

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.820
film to make, either.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:28.060
In one particularly gnarly scene, Lizzie has
a panic attack after vomiting maggots and

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.120
yellow bile all over a bus window.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.590
Director Richard Shepard told Bloody Disgusting
that that scene proved to be rather challenging:

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.620
"It was tough to edit because Logan is yelling
and freaking out so much.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.940
Just looking at takes was exhausting...But
I knew if we could get the sequence to work

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.150
it would be an amazing bit of movie-making."

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.760
Well, all that hard work certainly paid off.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:53.379
Viewers are obviously totally freaked out
by The Perfection, which is Certified Fresh

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.800
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:59.560
Many reviewers have praised the film, with
Katie Walsh of The Los Angeles Times claiming,

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.000
"The wild ride in store is both supremely
disturbing and unpredictable.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.500
But rendered with such care, skill and sheer
glee, it's utterly divine."

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:09.560
The A.V.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.540
Club's Katie Rife ultimately gave the film
a B minus, but also noted,

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:19.420
"The Perfection takes deep, fetishistic satisfaction
in pushing the envelope, then pushing it some

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:25.180
more, building in seductive fits and shocking
starts to an orgiastic frenzy of cinematic

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:25.940
excess."

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.920
The film definitely isn't for anyone with
a sensitive stomach...but if you're looking

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.570
for an original horror-thriller, go ahead
and check out The Perfection.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:37.300
Just be sure to have a barf bag at the ready…and
don't say we didn't warn you.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.880
"Help!

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.740
Help!"

